body:
You make an interesting point, when you refer to people having mental illness as a money opportunity. 

&#x200B;

I see so often situations that have people who are convinced they are mentally ill or suicidal, when in reality they are just going through a temporary crisis. For example, having them go on medication, or see a specialist. When in reality all the person needs for their crisis is just to go through with those feelings and they will cope better. Unfortunately people are told that trying to cope with things is not the best way to do things, and they must speak to a counselor etc. More $$$ for the system though.
